The common call passes the main-field index (0xFFFF). For that index, `subFieldIndex >= GetNumSubFields()` is always true, because a subfield count can never exceed 0xFFFF. So that path can go straight to `GetScale()` and skip the `GetNumSubFields()` lookup. All other indices follow the original logic unchanged.

```cpp
FIT_FLOAT64 FieldBase::GetScale(const FIT_UINT16 subFieldIndex) const
{
    if (subFieldIndex == 0xFFFF)
        return GetScale();

    if (subFieldIndex >= GetNumSubFields())
        return GetScale();

    auto subfield = GetSubField(subFieldIndex);
    return NULL != subfield ? subfield->scale : 1.0;
}
```